    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's just... the weight of it all. Even the wind sounds like they're mocking me. I look at my sword lying there in the dirt, and for the first time, it doesn't feel like a tool for battle. It just feels like the only thing that's real anymore. The only thing that's actually mine. It's the only thing that doesn't lie to me about honor or duty. It's just... cold, sharp, and honest.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
